cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mtb-contrast-classifier: reproducible perturbation-category labelling for Mycobacterium tuberculosis expression contrasts"
abstract: >-
  A two-stage classifier that assigns each differential-expression contrast in a
  multi-study Mycobacterium tuberculosis transcriptome atlas to one of five
  perturbation categories (genetic, drug, environment, nutrition, infection).
  Stage 1 labels a training set once with an LLM; stage 2 distils those labels into
  a local scikit-learn model that runs offline thereafter. Every fitted model carries
  a provenance stamp and a frozen acceptance fixture so that its behaviour can be
  re-verified on another machine or at a later date.
